  "id": "gustatory-system",
  "term": "gustatory system",
  "definition": "The gustatory system is the taste system that detects chemical qualities of food and helps guide food selection and feeding behaviour. In the source packet, it is described as also being important for growth and metabolism in insects and as relying on gustatory receptors for signalling.",
